+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Deleting a discontinued product currently invalidates carts and orders that reference it. Merchants and customers need deleted products removed from active carts while completed orders retain the exact purchased snapshot, so product lifecycle operations do not destroy transactional history.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Make product deletion safe for shopping carts: omit deleted items, recalculate quantities and totals, allow remaining-cart mutations and checkout, and reject new additions of deleted products with HTTP 404.
+- Preserve order-product snapshots independently of the catalog product, including SKU, name, quantity, price, subtotal, and order totals across all listed order read APIs and status updates.
+- Return HTTP 404 for deleted products from the v2 public SKU endpoint without affecting other products.
+- Add regression coverage for deletion, cart recovery/checkout, order reads/status changes, and deleted-product API behavior.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `deleted-product-lifecycle`: Defines safe behavior for deleted catalog products across carts, checkout, orders, and product retrieval.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+Affected catalog deletion and lookup services/controllers, shopping-cart persistence and calculation, checkout/order mapping and persistence, order API endpoints, and integration/unit tests across the Maven modules. Existing completed-order totals and product details must remain stable after catalog deletion.
