+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Catalog and cart deletion resilience
+
+- [x] 1.1 Trace and update product deletion and catalog lookup paths so a deleted product is absent from v2 SKU lookup with HTTP 404 while unrelated products continue to resolve; verify with product service/API tests.
+- [x] 1.2 Update shopping-cart service, item hydration, and calculation paths to filter deleted/missing products, remove their contribution from quantity/subtotal/total, and persist safe cart state; verify mixed-product and only-deleted-product cart tests.
+- [x] 1.3 Enforce deleted-product rejection in single and multi-add cart flows with HTTP 404, and ensure cart update/checkout paths use only live items; verify cart API and checkout tests including a cart containing only a deleted product.
+
+## 2. Order snapshot preservation
+
+- [x] 2.1 Trace order creation and order-product persistence/mapping and ensure SKU, name, quantity, purchase price, and subtotal are available from order-owned snapshot data without catalog dereferencing; verify order creation and persistence tests.
+- [x] 2.2 Update private and authenticated order single/list reads and merchant status updates to tolerate deleted catalog products while preserving product details and unchanged totals; verify all specified order endpoint tests.
+
+## 3. Regression integration coverage
+
+- [x] 3.1 Add an end-to-end regression scenario that creates a product, places it in a cart/order, deletes it, then exercises cart read/mutation/checkout, all order reads/status update, add rejection, and v2 SKU 404; verify with the targeted Maven integration test command.
+- [x] 3.2 Run the relevant module unit/integration test suites and inspect the diff for compatibility with live-product behavior; verify the selected Maven commands pass.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the completed OpenSpec change after implementation and verification.
